Feature: Task-ranked search order in kogen-context request
  A version 1 search request may carry "order": "ranked". kogen-context then
  ranks every matching line of the checkout: definitions and call sites in
  source code first, then other source lines, tests, generated code, comments
  and docs and other files last, and returns the first max_matches. Without
  "order", or with "order": "path", the packet is the unchanged version 1
  packet in path order. scripts/crane-replay.sh fetches two pinned public
  Crane revisions and records the ranks of both orders.

  Background:
    Given k-context-ranked-scoped-results: a checkout "kinds" with these files:
      | path                   | content |
      | README.md              | Use spin to wait.\n |
      | Makefile               | spin:\n\t./tools/run.py\n |
      | notes.txt              | spin notes\n |
      | lib/wait.zig           | /// spin waits for the goal.\n * spin in a block comment\npub fn spin() void {}\n |
      | src/loop.go            | package loop\n\n// spin waits.\nfunc spin(n int) int { return n }\n\nvar spinning = spin(4)\n\nfunc run() {\n\tx := spin (5) // spin again\n\ty := "fn spin(6)"\n\tz := 1 // then spin\n\t_, _, _ = x, y, z\n}\n |
      | src/spin_test.go       | package loop\n\nfunc TestSpin(t *testing.T) { spin(3) }\n |
      | src/generated/table.go | package generated\n\nvar table = spin(1)\n |
      | src/table.go           | package loop\n\n// Tables for the loop.\n//\n// Code generated by tablegen; DO NOT EDIT.\n\nvar t = spin(2)\n |
      | src/late.go            | package loop\n\nvar a = 1\nvar b = 2\nvar c = 3\n// DO NOT EDIT: this line is too late to mark the file.\nvar late = spin(7)\n |
      | tools/run.py           | #!/usr/bin/env python3\n# spin from the shell\ndef spin():\n    return print("// spin")\n\n\nspin()\n |
      | web/app.spec.ts        | spin();\n |
