      """
      # Sweeps

      A sweep cuts its worklist into chunks and runs each chunk on several runners.
      Each runner writes journal.shard<k>.jsonl in the chunk's directory.
      A chunk with one runner writes journal.jsonl instead of journal.shard0.jsonl.
      The site reads every journal.shard*.jsonl it finds.
      Collect journal.shard*.wptreport.jsonl for the per-subtest results.
      Do not count journal.shard*.wptreport.jsonl as a journal.
      A resumed sweep keeps each chunk's journal.shard files.
      The runner's heartbeat file is journal.shard<k>.jsonl.heartbeat.
      Remove journal.shard files only with their chunk.
      """
    And k-context-ranked-scoped-results: the file "tests/ranking/wpt/docs/lessons/stream-names.md" of the repository holds exactly:
      """
      # A chunk names its stream by its runner count

      **Lesson**: a chunk with several runners writes journal.shard<k>.wptreport.jsonl.
      **Why**: each runner streams beside its own journal.shard<k>.jsonl.
      **What Happened**: a reader globbed journal.shard*.jsonl and missed one-runner chunks.
      **Fix**: read both journal.jsonl and journal.shard*.jsonl.
      **Takeaway**: journal.shard is the several-runner layout.
      """
    And k-context-ranked-scoped-results: the file "tests/ranking/wpt/tests/runner/main.zig" of the repository holds exactly:
      """
      //! The WPT runner: splits the worklist into shards and runs each on its own runner.

      const std = @import("std");

      pub fn runShards(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, dir: []const u8, shard_count: u32) !void {
          var i: u32 = 0;
          while (i < shard_count) : (i += 1) {
              // Each shard keeps its own journal (journal.shard<i>.jsonl).
              const jl = try std.fmt.allocPrint(allocator, "{s}/journal.shard{d}.jsonl", .{ dir, i });
              defer allocator.free(jl);
          }
      }
      """
